{"title":"Career Roadmap · Pharmacist","role":"Pharmacist","summary":"A Pharmacist is a healthcare professional who works with medicines, including their preparation, dispensing, storage, quality, safe use, patient counselling and medication-related information.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Pharm (Bachelor of Pharmacy)","Course":"Pharmaceutical Sciences"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A Pharmacist is a healthcare professional who works with medicines, including their preparation, dispensing, storage, quality, safe use, patient counselling and medication-related information."},{"type":"p","text":"For a B.Pharm graduate in India, career opportunities span:"},{"type":"h","text":"Community pharmacy"},{"type":"h","text":"Hospital pharmacy"},{"type":"h","text":"Clinical pharmacy support"},{"type":"h","text":"Pharmaceutical manufacturing"},{"type":"h","text":"Quality control"},{"type":"h","text":"Quality assurance"},{"type":"h","text":"Regulatory affairs"},{"type":"h","text":"Pharmacovigilance"},{"type":"h","text":"Medical information"},{"type":"h","text":"Clinical research"},{"type":"h","text":"Pharmaceutical sales and marketing"},{"type":"h","text":"Drug distribution and supply chain"},{"type":"h","text":"Pharmacy administration"},{"type":"h","text":"Healthcare technology"},{"type":"p","text":"For a career specifically titled Pharmacist, the student must complete the applicable registration and professional requirements under the current Indian pharmacy regulatory framework. A B.Pharm degree alone should not be treated as automatic authorization to practise as a registered pharmacist."}]},{"heading":"Career Pathway","kind":"growth","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"B.Pharm"},{"type":"h","text":"Industrial / Hospital / Community Pharmacy Training"},{"type":"h","text":"Applicable Pharmacist Registration"},{"type":"h","text":"Registered Pharmacist / Pharmacy Role"},{"type":"h","text":"P